<title>USA: Motorist group says N.Calif. retail gasoline falls.</title>
<headline>Motorist group says N.Calif. retail gasoline falls.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Retail gas prices in northern California dropped significantly in October, the California State Automobile Association (CSAA) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The average price for self-serve unleaded gasoline was $1.36 a gallon in northern California, down eleven cents from CSAA's September 19, Fuel Gauge Survey.</p>
<p>&quot;Gas prices in northern California appear to be taking their usual autumn drop with the end of the summer driving season and less demand for gasoline,&quot; said CSAA spokesman Ron Kennedy.</p>
<p>The average for self-serve unleaded varies dramatically, the association said.</p>
</text>
